# packages/mastra type-check baseline (S261-S2)
#
# Pre-existing `tsc -p packages/mastra` error count on origin/main at story time
# (tip 6f1a508, the task-audit merge). This file exists so the mastra type-check can
# join the root `pnpm type-check` gate WITHOUT fixing main's errors in this PR
# (no-scope-creep rule). Ratchet the number DOWN as test-file typings are fixed;
# never ratchet it UP without calling it out in review.
#
# The 22 errors are all in src/**/*.test.ts (loose test-fixture typings):
#   observability/map-span.test.ts            7  (TS2352/TS2353 SpanErrorInfo/UsageStats casts)
#   observability/resolve-span-error-text.test.ts 6  (TS2353/TS2741 SpanErrorInfo shapes)
#   abort-clears-running.test.ts              2  (TS2353/TS2339)
#   qwen-plain-user-guard.test.ts             2  (TS2339 on never)
#   observability/tourbillon-postgres-exporter.test.ts 2 (TS2353 UsageStats)
#   concierge-signal.test.ts                  1  (TS2322)
#   execution-workspace.test.ts               1  (TS1360 AgentRuntimeConfig literal)
#   observability/assistant-tracing.test.ts   1  (TS2322 fake model stream)
# Production sources (src/**/*.ts excluding tests) are ERROR-FREE under this tsconfig.
#
# Why the tsconfig differs from the scheduler's: no `rootDir` (the scheduler's
# `rootDir: src` + root tsconfig.base `paths` produce ~140 TS6059 errors from
# cross-package sources; omitting it keeps mastra covered without inheriting that
# structural noise), `lib` adds DOM (fetch/ReadableStream/FormData globals the
# package uses), `types: ["node"]` is explicit because TypeScript 6.0 does not
# auto-include @types/node here.
22
